# CITATION.cff (Citation File Format 1.2.0)
# https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# This file enables GitHub's "Cite this repository" feature and lets tools
# such as Zenodo, JOSS, Zotero, and Mendeley generate consistent citations
# of Solidum FEM.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Solidum FEM in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Solidum FEM"
abstract: >-
  A displacement-based finite element framework for research in solid
  mechanics: simulation of mechanical and thermal problems (heat conduction
  is currently uncoupled from the mechanical field), with an architecture
  optimized for extension via AI-assisted development. The main program
  provides 1D structural elements (2- and 3-node truss, cable, frame with an
  optional fiber section), 2D and 3D solid elements, elastic (isotropic and
  orthotropic), J2 and Drucker-Prager plasticity, continuum damage and
  uniaxial confined concrete materials, interface laws (mode I and
  mixed-mode cohesive damage, bar-concrete bond-slip), embedded
  reinforcement with perfect bond or bond-slip, linear and nonlinear static
  solvers with load stages, cylindrical arc-length, indirect displacement
  control, modal analysis, Newmark and HHT time integration, central
  difference, harmonic response, and response spectrum analysis. Heat
  conduction is supported in steady state and transient regimes, in 2D and
  3D. Non-standard formulations are written as user modules, in
  solidum/user/<name>/, and loaded explicitly by the model that needs them:
  an embedded strong discontinuity element with crack tracking, and a
  dissipation-based arc-length control.

authors:
